## Why This Is Asked

Gauges ability to design end-to-end CAPA artifacts for data exposure in multi-tenant data platforms.

## Key Concepts

- CAPA data modeling
- Lifecycle state machines
- API design for incident records
- Telemetry and tenant-scoped metrics
- RCA templates and Canary remediation

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal REST handler sketch for creating a CAPA
app.post('/caps', (req, res) => {
  const { cap_id, incident, tenant_id, evidence } = req.body;
  if (!cap_id || !tenant_id) return res.status(400).send('Missing fields');
  // store CAPA entry
  res.status(201).json({ cap_id, status: 'created' });
});
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test the CAPA under concurrent backup runs?
- What metrics would you monitor to ensure containment over time?

## Why This Is Asked

Assess ability to design end-to-end CAPA for a secrets rotation bug with tenant isolation across regions, including data capture, lifecycle, APIs, metrics, and rollout controls.

## Key Concepts

- CAPA data model capturing tenant context, vault/version, exposure window, evidence, remediation.
- Region-aware lifecycle with states: detected, contained, eradicated, verified, closed.
- Minimal REST API: create/update CAPA, link logs/traces, idempotent operations.
- Metrics: recurrence rate, MTTR per region, false-positive rate, time-to-containment.
- RCA template and canary rollout validation plan before global deployment.

## Code Example

```javascript
type CAPA = {
  id: string;
  incidentId: string;
  tenantId: string;
  vaultVersion: string;
  exposureWindowMs: number;
  evidenceLinks: string[];
  remediation: string;
  state: "detected" | "contained" | "eradicated" | "verified" | "closed";
  region: string;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate the rotation gate cannot be bypassed in CI/CD pipelines?
- Which metrics best differentiate false positives from real exposures, and how would you alert on them?
- What logging/tracing strategy ties CAPAs to specific secrets and Vault rotations across regions?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a CAPA program around operational risk in alert routing, including change control, cross-tenant impact, and measurable containment.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model (evidence, lineage, owners)
- Lifecycle with detect/contain/remediate/verify and SLAs
- Canary-based rollback and change control
- Metrics: containment time, recurrence rate, MTTR

## Code Example
```javascript
// Express-like minimal CAPA create endpoint (illustrative)
app.post('/caps', (req, res) => {
  const capa = req.body;
  // persist CAPA with evidence, lineage, owners
  res.status(201).send({ id: 'capa-123', ...capa });
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test the canary rollback plan for alert-rule changes?
- What telemetry would you collect to validate containment and prevent recurrence?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to translate a data-path incident into a systematic CAPA plan, from data model to evidence mgmt and preventive action. Evaluates clarity, traceability, and practical canary-based rollout.

## Key Concepts

- CAPA data model
- State machine
- Evidence management and RCA
- Region-aware metrics
- Canary-based remediation

## Code Example

```javascript
// Type definitions for CAPA (illustrative)
type CAPA = {
  id: string;
  title: string;
  description: string;
  evidence: string[];
  rootCause: string;
  correctiveAction: string;
  preventiveAction: string;
  status: 'proposed'|'in_progress'|'implemented'|'verified'|'closed';
  region: string;
  severity: 'low'|'medium'|'high';
  createdAt: string;
  updatedAt: string;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you structure region-aware metrics and dashboards?
- What RCAs templates and safeguards would you require before closing a CAPA?
